<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN ELECTRORAIL SLIPS INTO LOSS.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN ELECTRORAIL SLIPS INTO LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net loss			43.9  vs    147.9 profit</p>
<p>    Cons cash flow		     30.7  vs     14.5</p>
<p>    Cons shareholders equity	 47.5  vs     91.8</p>
<p>    Cons balance sheet total    1,194.8  vs  1,519.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Real estate company Electrorail said in a statement</p>
<p>profits were affected by a 50 million franc write-down. After</p>
<p>costs and interest rents received were positive and the company</p>
<p>said the improvement in revenue would benefit cash flows in 1997</p>
<p>and 1998. Bank debts fell by 44 million francs.</p>
<p>The company said it was studying new projects which would</p>
<p>boost profitability. It could not be excluded that developing</p>
<p>the company further would involve a partner, it added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
